# Focused transport-provider matrix for parallel ownership.
#
# The green-channel and capability rows execute the current pure-Simple owners.
# Native/Crossbeam/value-channel rows are source-bound until an admitted
# self-hosted native runner is available; they must not be called live evidence.

"""Focused bounded transport provider matrix.

## Overview

The GreenChannel and ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1 rows execute current
pure-Simple owners. Native/Crossbeam/value-channel rows inspect and bind the
real Rust/C owners only; they do not claim native, process, device, or live
transport evidence until an admitted self-hosted native runner executes them.

**Requirements:** doc/02_requirements/feature/parallel_ownership_memory_layout.md
**Plan:** doc/03_plan/sys_test/parallel_ownership_memory_layout.md
**Design:** doc/05_design/language/concurrency/parent_commit_parallel_apps.md
**Research:** doc/01_research/language/parallel_ownership_and_storage_layout_research_2026-08-12.md

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/common/structural/parallel_transport_provider_matrix_spec.spl --mode=interpreter` with an admitted self-hosted CLI. The current bootstrap-seed attempt is BLOCKED by compiler parser work, so these scenarios are contract/source evidence rather than a native release PASS.

## Limitations

This matrix does not prove separate-process isolation, device execution, or a
source-matched native provider. Capability registry calls are pure-Simple model
evidence until a runtime/process owner integrates the registry.

## Purpose and audience

This manual is for runtime maintainers, assurance reviewers, and release
operators deciding whether a channel or actor provider may carry data across an
execution boundary. It distinguishes executable pure-Simple model evidence,
source-bound provider checks, focused Rust/C unit evidence, and unavailable
native or separate-process evidence.

## Preconditions

1. Work from the repository root.
2. Use an admitted exact-current self-hosted `bin/simple` for an execution
   verdict. The Rust bootstrap seed is diagnostic only.
3. Keep the runtime source tree and selected runtime archive identity manifest
   unchanged during the run.
4. Do not substitute fixture, screenshot, cached, or source-only evidence for a
   native/process receipt.
5. Preserve bounded timeout and capture settings from the SPipe runner.

## Syntax and interfaces

`green_channel_new(capacity)` creates a finite pure-Simple reference channel.
`green_channel_send(channel, value)` returns an updated channel plus explicit
sent/backpressure/closed fields. `green_channel_close_drain(channel)` closes
admission but preserves buffered FIFO values. `ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1`
mints owner-bound one-shot immutable handle capabilities; `validate` consumes a
matching live capability and rejects replay.

The C scalar provider owns `rt_channel_*` and typed-i64 helpers. Rust object
channels own `rt_value_channel_*`. Actor admission uses stable status codes for
accepted, full, closed, invalid, and cancelled outcomes. These namespaces are
not interchangeable.

## Execution

```text
bin/simple test test/01_unit/common/structural/parallel_transport_provider_matrix_spec.spl --mode=interpreter
```

Expected release evidence is a real test receipt from an admitted self-hosted
CLI. The current retained attempt stopped before scenario loading on compiler
parser work, so this document does not claim that receipt.

## Provider matrix

| Provider | Bound | Payload admission | Current evidence |
|---|---:|---|---|
| GreenChannel reference | caller capacity | integer model | executable model scenarios |
| C scalar channel | 1024 | tagged scalar / typed i64 | direct C selfcheck + source binding |
| Rust object channel | 1024 | inline RuntimeValue subset | focused Rust tests + source binding |
| Compiler Crossbeam | 1024 | recursively immutable Value | focused Rust provider tests |
| Actor mailbox | 64 | inline value envelope | focused Rust actor tests |
| Object capability registry | configured fixed slots | frozen object handle | pure-Simple model; runtime wiring pending |

## Scenario interpretation

Capacity-plus-one must reject without growth. Closing must stop new sends while
allowing buffered values to drain in FIFO order. A parked receiver must be
woken by cancellation. Mutable dynamic values and pointer-like handles must
reject before queue admission. A minted object capability succeeds once; wrong
owner, wrong target, stale generation, forged token, replay, and revoked state
must reject without consuming another live slot.

## Findings and scorecard

| Quality dimension | Score | Finding |
|---|---:|---|
| Executable assertions | 5/5 | scenarios contain concrete state/result checks |
| Stub freedom | 5/5 | docgen reports zero stubs |
| Requirement traceability | 5/5 | REQ-PAR-002/005/006 are named |
| Provider coverage | 4/5 | source/focused coverage; no admitted native process run |
| Failure semantics | 5/5 | full/closed/cancel/invalid/replay are distinct |
| Operator usability | 4/5 | exact command present; admitted CLI unavailable |
| Release evidence | 1/5 | intentionally blocked pending self-hosted/native/process receipts |

## Provenance

Canonical source is
`test/01_unit/common/structural/parallel_transport_provider_matrix_spec.spl`.
The generated manual is
`doc/06_spec/01_unit/common/structural/parallel_transport_provider_matrix_spec.md`.
Architecture, design, plan, requirements, research, guide, bug records, and
SPipe state are authoritative at `doc/04_architecture/language/parallel_ownership_model.md`,
`doc/07_guide/language/parallel_apps.md`,
`doc/08_tracking/bug/parallel_runtime_raw_value_transport_2026-08-12.md`, and
`.spipe/parallel_ownership_memory_layout/state.md`. Docgen completion and
stub count are retained in the SPipe state log; they are documentation evidence,
not transport execution evidence.

## Compatibility and limitations

The legacy void actor send remains compatibility-only; assurance callers use
the result-bearing hook. Scalar and object channel ABIs intentionally differ in
representation and symbol namespace. The capability registry is a value-only
model and does not yet authenticate a real process receiver. No scenario here
proves graph cloning, remote codec interoperability, device leases, process ID
isolation, or cancellation rollback across a kernel process boundary.

## Recovery

If source parsing fails, repair the named compiler owner and rerun this one
focused command in a fresh bounded session. If a native provider differs from
the reference result, reject the provider rather than weakening the scenario.
If archive identity validation fails, rebuild the runtime archive and its
SHA-256 identity manifest from the exact unchanged runtime source tree.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.io.file_read_text
use std.concurrent.green_channel.{
    green_channel_new,
    green_channel_len,
    green_channel_backpressure_count,
    green_channel_is_closed,
    green_channel_close_drain,
    green_channel_recv,
    green_channel_send
}
use std.common.structural.transfer.transfer_contracts.{
    TransferEnvelopeV1,
    ParallelExecutionDomain,
    ParallelTransferMode,
    ParallelTransferPayload,
    transfer_envelope_v1
}
use std.common.structural.transfer.object_handle_capability_registry.{
    ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1
}

describe "Parallel ownership bounded transport provider matrix":

    describe "REQ-PAR-006 bounded transport":
        it "rejects capacity plus one and records backpressure":
            val first = green_channel_send(green_channel_new(2), 11)
            val second = green_channel_send(first.channel, 22)
            val third = green_channel_send(second.channel, 33)
            expect(first.sent).to_be(true)
            expect(second.sent).to_be(true)
            expect(third.sent).to_be(false)
            expect(third.backpressure).to_be(true)
            expect(third.reason).to_equal("bounded_backpressure")
            expect(green_channel_len(third.channel)).to_equal(2)
            expect(green_channel_backpressure_count(third.channel)).to_equal(1)

        it "preserves queued values while the bounded queue reports pressure":
            val first = green_channel_send(green_channel_new(2), 7)
            val second = green_channel_send(first.channel, 8)
            val rejected = green_channel_send(second.channel, 9)
            val received = green_channel_recv(rejected.channel, 1)
            expect(received.received).to_be(true)
            expect(received.value).to_equal(7)
            expect(green_channel_len(received.channel)).to_equal(1)
            expect(green_channel_backpressure_count(received.channel)).to_equal(1)

        it "keeps the bounded capacity after a receive makes room":
            val first = green_channel_send(green_channel_new(1), 41)
            val received = green_channel_recv(first.channel, 3)
            val accepted = green_channel_send(received.channel, 42)
            expect(received.value).to_equal(41)
            expect(accepted.sent).to_be(true)
            expect(accepted.backpressure).to_be(false)
            expect(green_channel_len(accepted.channel)).to_equal(1)

    describe "REQ-PAR-006 close and cancellation":
        it "drains buffered values before returning CLOSED":
            val sent = green_channel_send(green_channel_new(2), 55)
            val closed = green_channel_close_drain(sent.channel)
            val drained = green_channel_recv(closed.channel, 10)
            val terminal = green_channel_recv(drained.channel, 11)
            expect(green_channel_is_closed(closed.channel)).to_be(true)
            expect(drained.received).to_be(true)
            expect(drained.value).to_equal(55)
            expect(drained.channel_closed).to_be(false)
            expect(terminal.received).to_be(false)
            expect(terminal.parked).to_be(false)
            expect(terminal.channel_closed).to_be(true)
            expect(terminal.reason).to_equal("channel_closed")

        it "wakes parked receivers and leaves no waiter after cancellation":
            val parked = green_channel_recv(green_channel_new(1), 71)
            val closed = green_channel_close_drain(parked.channel)
            expect(parked.parked).to_be(true)
            expect(closed.woken_task_ids.len()).to_equal(1)
            expect(closed.woken_task_ids[0]).to_equal(71)
            expect(green_channel_is_closed(closed.channel)).to_be(true)
            expect(green_channel_recv(closed.channel, 72).channel_closed).to_be(true)

        it "rejects sends after close as cancellation rather than pressure":
            val closed = green_channel_close_drain(green_channel_new(1))
            val rejected = green_channel_send(closed.channel, 99)
            expect(rejected.sent).to_be(false)
            expect(rejected.channel_closed).to_be(true)
            expect(rejected.backpressure).to_be(false)
            expect(rejected.reason).to_equal("channel_closed")

    describe "REQ-PAR-005 typed transport admission":
        it "keeps mutable dynamic values fail-closed in the native provider owner":
            val source = file_read_text(
                "src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/interpreter_extern/concurrency.rs")
            expect(source).to_contain("Value::FrozenArray(values) => values.iter().all(is_admitted)")
            expect(source).to_contain("_ => false")
            expect(source).to_contain("admit_dynamic_transport(&value)?")

        it "binds the Crossbeam provider to the same finite capacity":
            val source = file_read_text(
                "src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/concurrent_providers/native_impl.rs")
            expect(source).to_contain("pub const NATIVE_CHANNEL_CAPACITY: usize = 1024")
            expect(source).to_contain("crossbeam::channel::bounded(NATIVE_CHANNEL_CAPACITY)")
            expect(source).to_contain("TrySendError::Full")

        it "binds the scalar C provider to fixed capacity without growth":
            val source = file_read_text("src/runtime/runtime_native.c")
            expect(source).to_contain("if (ch->count == ch->capacity)")
            expect(source).to_contain("return 0;")
            expect(source).to_contain("ch->capacity = 1024")

        it "binds the Rust object provider to its distinct bounded namespace":
            val source = file_read_text(
                "src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/channels.rs")
            expect(source).to_contain("rt_value_channel_new")
            expect(source).to_contain("RUNTIME_CHANNEL_CAPACITY")
            expect(source).to_contain("try_send")

        it "binds typed scalar helpers and object lifecycle race evidence":
            val c_source = file_read_text("src/runtime/runtime_native.c")
            val rust_source = file_read_text(
                "src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/channels.rs")
            expect(c_source).to_contain("rt_channel_send_i64")
            expect(c_source).to_contain("rt_channel_classify_any")
            expect(rust_source).to_contain("Arc<RuntimeChannelState>")
            expect(rust_source).to_contain("concurrent_free_with_send_close_and_queries")

        it "binds actor capacity admission and explicit result statuses":
            val common = file_read_text("src/compiler_rust/common/src/actor.rs")
            val runtime = file_read_text("src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/actors.rs")
            val hook = file_read_text("src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/concurrent/actor_hooks.spl")
            expect(common).to_contain("ACTOR_MAILBOX_CAPACITY: usize = 64")
            expect(runtime).to_contain("rt_actor_send_result")
            expect(runtime).to_contain("ActorSendStatus::Full")
            expect(hook).to_contain("actor_hook_send_result")

        it "retains explicit mutable rejection and immutable acceptance evidence":
            val source = file_read_text(
                "src/compiler_rust/compiler/tests/concurrent_providers_test.rs")
            expect(source).to_contain("native_channel_transport_rejects_mutable_dynamic_values")
            expect(source).to_contain("native_channel_transport_accepts_recursive_immutable_payloads")
            expect(source).to_contain("native_channel_capacity_plus_one_is_rejected_without_blocking")

    describe "REQ-PAR-002 and REQ-PAR-005 capability lifecycle":
        it "accepts a minted process capability once and rejects replay":
            var registry = ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1.create(101, 2)
            val minted = registry.mint(8, 3, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process)
            val envelope = transfer_envelope_v1(8, 3,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token, false)
            expect(minted.ok).to_be(true)
            expect(registry.validate(envelope, 101)).to_be(true)
            expect(registry.validate(envelope, 101)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.live_count()).to_equal(0)

        it "rejects forged and stale capabilities before consuming a live slot":
            var registry = ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1.create(202, 2)
            val minted = registry.mint(9, 4, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process)
            val forged = transfer_envelope_v1(9, 4,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token + 1, false)
            val stale = transfer_envelope_v1(9, 5,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token, false)
            expect(registry.validate(forged, 202)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.validate(stale, 202)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.live_count()).to_equal(1)
            expect(registry.validate(
                transfer_envelope_v1(9, 4,
                    ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                    ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                    minted.handle.ownership_token, false),
                202)).to_be(true)

        it "rejects wrong owner and wrong target without weakening the boundary":
            var registry = ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1.create(303, 2)
            val minted = registry.mint(10, 1, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process)
            val wrong_owner = transfer_envelope_v1(10, 1,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token, false)
            val wrong_target = transfer_envelope_v1(10, 1,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Device,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare,
                ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token, false)
            expect(registry.validate(wrong_owner, 304)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.validate(wrong_target, 303)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.live_count()).to_equal(1)

        it "rejects a revoked capability without consuming another slot":
            var registry = ObjectHandleCapabilityRegistryV1.create(404, 2)
            val minted = registry.mint(11, 2, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process)
            val envelope = transfer_envelope_v1(11, 2,
                ParallelExecutionDomain.Parent, ParallelExecutionDomain.Process,
                ParallelTransferMode.FrozenShare, ParallelTransferPayload.ObjectHandle,
                minted.handle.ownership_token, false)
            expect(registry.revoke(minted.handle, 404)).to_be(true)
            expect(registry.validate(envelope, 404)).to_be(false)
            expect(registry.live_count()).to_equal(0)
